    74	## 2. Registry
    75	
    76	### 2.1 Coordination (F-01, F-02)
    77	
    78	O_EXCL lock with `ProcessInstanceIdentityV1` from `STD-TURNLOCK-RUNNER-COORDINATION`.
    79	Liveness verified via signed-challenge probe, not `kill(pid, 0)`.
    80	
    81	**Lock acquisition:**
    82	
    83	```typescript
    84	class RegistryLock {
    85	  acquire(root: string, policy: DelegationResourcePolicyV2): void {
    86	    // O_EXCL open, write ProcessInstanceIdentityV1, fsync
    87	    // On EEXIST: read holder identity
    88	    //   If holder identity fails signed-challenge probe → stale
    89	    //   Throw "registry-locked" with holderIdentity in details
    90	    //   (Do NOT unlink. recovery via recoverRegistry().)
    91	    // Retry up to policy.lockTimeoutMs
    92	  }
    93	
    94	  release(): void {
    95	    // inode = fs.fstatSync(this.fd).ino
    96	    // currentInode = fs.statSync(this.path).ino
    97	    // if (inode !== currentInode) → do NOT unlink (replaced)
    98	    // fs.closeSync(this.fd)
    99	    // fs.unlinkSync(this.path)
   100	  }
   101	}
   102	```
   103	
   104	**recoverRegistry (F-02):**
   105	
   106	```typescript
   107	function recoverRegistry(proofOfDeath: ArtifactCommitmentV2): { recovered: boolean } {
   108	  // Read lock file → extract holder ProcessInstanceIdentityV1
   109	  // Validate proofOfDeath against holder identity
   110	  // If valid AND holder fails liveness probe:
   111	  //   unlink lock file, initialize recovery
   112	  //   return { recovered: true }
   113	  // return { recovered: false }
   114	}
   115	```
