   218	
   219	### 3.2 Path resolution (F-04b)
   220	
   221	All paths are resolved relative to `registryRoot`. The implementation
   222	provides `ArtifactRootBindingV1` mappings (e.g., `"turnlock-run"` →
   223	`registryRoot`) at initialization time.
   224	
   225	**Safe-open traversal:** Before writing to a `rawResultTarget`, resolve the
   226	path component by component. For each component from the root:
   227	1. Verify the component is not `..` and contains no `/` or `\0`.
   228	2. Construct the intermediate path.
   229	3. `fs.statSync` the intermediate path.
   230	4. If `stat.isSymbolicLink()` → reject (symlink anywhere in chain).
   231	5. Continue to next component.
   232	6. For the final component: `fs.openSync(path, "wx", 0o600)` — this also
   233	   enforces write-once (fails if exists).
   234	
   235	No `realpathSync` (follows symlinks). No `O_NOFOLLOW` on the final component
   236	alone (doesn't protect parent directories).
   237	
   238	---
   239	
   240	## 4. Claim Fencing (F-03)
   241	
   242	### 4.1 Under-lock atomic claim
   243	
   244	Child startup under coordination lock (same as §2.1):
   245	
   246	1. Acquire lock.
   247	2. Read `fenceGeneration`. If `>= generation` → release, exit(0).
   248	3. Write claim: `ProcessInstanceIdentityV1` + generation + nonce +
   249	   livenessEndpoint. `fsync`.
   250	4. Release lock.
   251	5. Record `PGID` (`process.getpgid(0)`) in registry.
   252	
   253	### 4.2 Heartbeat fence re-verification
   254	
   255	Child runs a periodic heartbeat (interval = `ownerHeartbeatMs / 3`):
   256	
   257	1. Respond to parent's signed-challenge probe via liveness socket.
   258	2. Re-acquire lock (non-blocking try).
   259	3. Read `fenceGeneration`. If `>= generation`: release lock, auto-terminate
   260	   before any I/O operation.
   261	4. Release lock.
   262	
   263	This prevents the scenario where G1 is suspended (SIGSTOP), G2 fences and
   264	spawns, then G1 resumes: G1's next heartbeat detects the fence and exits.
   265	
   266	### 4.3 Indeterminate liveness
   267	
   268	A launcher that misses heartbeats but whose PID is still alive is
   269	**indeterminate** — not dead. The provider MUST NOT fence. The caller may:
   270	
   271	- Call `stopLaunch` (SIGKILL to the PGID) → guaranteed termination.
   272	- Wait for the launcher to resume heartbeats.
   273	- If the PID eventually dies → stale-run reconciliation declares it dead.
   274	
   275	---
   276	
   277	## 5. Launcher Process Management
   278	
   279	### 5.1 Spawn (F-04c)
   280	
   281	Uses the sessionless engine (prerequisite, §0.1):
   282	
   283	1. Map `ResolvedJobPlanV2[]` to engine input format.
   284	2. Pass Turnlock env vars: `PI_TURNLOCK_LAUNCH_KEY`, `PI_TURNLOCK_GENERATION`,
   285	   `PI_TURNLOCK_NONCE`, `PI_TURNLOCK_REGISTRY_ROOT`.
   286	3. Child entry point (`turnlock/launcher-entry.ts`):
   287	   a. Parse env vars.
   288	   b. Execute claim protocol (§4.1).
   289	   c. Open liveness socket for signed-challenge probe.
   290	   d. Start heartbeat loop (§4.2).
   291	   e. Execute agent instructions via sessionless engine.
   292	   f. Write result envelopes to `ArtifactTargetRefV1` paths (via safe-open).
   293	
   294	### 5.2 Stop (F-03)
   295	
   296	Target the persisted `PGID`:
   297	1. SIGTERM → `-pgid`.
   298	2. Wait `stopRequestMs`.
   299	3. SIGKILL → `-pgid`.
   300	4. Wait `stopRequestMs`.
   301	5. `pgrep -g <pgid>` → iterate survivors, test liveness.
   302	6. Survivors after `stopReconciliationMs` → `unresolvedOrphans`.
   303	
   304	---
   305	
   306	## 6. Result Envelopes
   307	
   308	### 6.1 Universal envelope
   309	
   310	Per STD §6. Launcher writes `JobSuccessEnvelope` / `JobFailureEnvelope`.
   311	Reconciler writes `JobFailureEnvelope` for launcher-died cases.
   312	Stop handler writes `JobStoppedEnvelope`.
   313	
   314	### 6.2 Path confinement (F-04b)
   315	
   316	All result writes use safe-open traversal (§3.2). `..` rejected at resolution.
   317	Symlinks rejected at any path component.
   318	
   319	### 6.3 Integrity
   320	
   321	`readJobResult`: SHA-256 of file bytes. Mismatch with `resultCommitment` →
   322	`"integrity-conflict"`. Never update the registry's commitment silently.
   323	
   324	---
   325	
   326	## 7. Retention Lifecycle (F-06)
   327	
   328	### 7.1 Per-artifact states
   329	
   330	```
   331	terminal → receipt → delete-intent → deleted → tombstone
   332	```
   333	
   334	- **receipt**: `acknowledgeRetention` recorded.
   335	- **delete-intent**: Collector will delete.
   336	- **deleted**: File removed.
   337	- **tombstone**: Expiry set to
   338	  `earliestCleanupAtEpochMs + max(retentionFloorMs, terminalRetentionDays × 86_400_000)`.
   339	  Entry removed after expiry.
   340	
   341	### 7.2 Cursor-based collector
   342	
   343	```typescript
   344	class ResultCollector {
   345	  private timer: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;
   346	  private disposed = false;
   347	
   348	  start(policy: DelegationResourcePolicyV2): void {
   349	    this.timer = setInterval(() => this.collect(), policy.observationPollMs);
   350	    this.timer.unref();
   351	  }
   352	
   353	  private collect(): void {
   354	    if (this.disposed) return;
   355	    const lock = this.registry.acquireLock();
   356	    try {
   357	      const cursor = this.registry.readCursor();
   358	      const batch = this.registry.scanRetentionCandidates(cursor, 100);
   359	      let dirty = false;
   360	      for (const entry of batch) {
   361	        for (const [jobId, job] of Object.entries(entry.jobs)) {
   362	          // 1. Transition receipt → delete-intent (persist BEFORE unlink)
   363	          if (job.retentionState === "receipt" &&
   364	              Date.now() >= job.retentionReceipt!.earliestCleanupAtEpochMs) {
   365	            job.retentionState = "delete-intent";
   366	            job.deleteIntentAtEpochMs = Date.now();
   367	            dirty = true;
   368	          }
   369	        }
   370	      }
   371	      // Persist delete-intent transitions before any unlink
   372	      if (dirty) this.registry.writeBatch(batch);
   373	      // 2. Delete files for delete-intent jobs, then persist deleted
   374	      dirty = false;
   375	      for (const entry of batch) {
   376	        for (const [jobId, job] of Object.entries(entry.jobs)) {
   377	          if (job.retentionState === "delete-intent") {
   378	            try { fs.unlinkSync(this.resolveTarget(job.targetRef)); }
   379	            catch (err) { if (err.code !== "ENOENT") throw err; }
   380	            job.retentionState = "deleted";
   381	            job.deletedAtEpochMs = Date.now();
   382	            dirty = true;
   383	          }
   384	        }
   385	        // 3. Transition deleted → tombstone when all jobs done
   386	        if (Object.values(entry.jobs).every(j =>
   387	            j.retentionState === "deleted" || j.retentionState === "tombstone")) {
   388	          for (const job of Object.values(entry.jobs)) {
   389	            if (job.retentionState === "deleted") {
   390	              job.retentionState = "tombstone";
   391	              job.tombstoneExpiryAtEpochMs =
   392	                Date.now() +
   393	                Math.max(policy.retentionFloorMs,
   394	                         policy.terminalRetentionDays * 86_400_000);
   395	              dirty = true;
   396	            }
   397	          }
   398	        }
   399	      }
   400	      // 4. Persist cursor + deleted states atomically (after unlink)
   401	      if (dirty || batch.length > 0) {
   402	        this.registry.writeCursorAndBatch(batch.lastKey, batch);
   403	      }
   404	    } finally {
   405	      lock.release();
   406	    }
   407	  }
   408	
   409	  dispose(): void {
   410	    this.disposed = true;
   411	    if (this.timer) { clearInterval(this.timer); this.timer = null; }
   412	  }
   413	}
   414	```
   415	
   416	### 7.3 Crash safety
   417	
   418	Registry shows: receipt, some delete-intent, some deleted. Collector resumes
   419	from cursor. `acknowledgeRetention` retry → existing receipt → success.
   420	`readJobResult` for tombstoned job → `"job-not-found"` with
   421	`details: { reason: "released" }`.
   422	
